 terminal  tmux 3.4 → xterm-256color, 214×54, SSH   colour 256 colours (tmux client without RGB, xterm-256color)   background dark (tmux OSC 11)
 links     OSC 8 ✗ (tmux client without hyperlinks)   underline curly ✗ (tmux client without usstyle)   images blocks(half) — kitty ✗ client lacks RGB · sixel ✗ client lacks sixel
 probe     tmux answered in 2 ms   cell size unknown (client cell 0x0)
 warn      tmux's client reports no 24-bit colour: images and colours are rounded to 256 (likely mosh or an older terminal); for full colour use SSH, or `set -as terminal-features ',xterm-256color:RGB'` if your terminal supports it
 warn      images are block characters: tmux's client has no way to show pixels (no RGB for kitty placeholders, no sixel); likely mosh, which carries text only: use SSH for pixels
 warn      links are not clickable: tmux's client has no hyperlinks feature (likely mosh, which drops them); `set -as terminal-features ',xterm-256color:hyperlinks'` if your terminal shows OSC 8 links
